Actually wait — with drainMs: 0 and subagent active: my new action returns `drain` (legacy uncapped). The round: `Future.wait([jobManager.settled])` vs `_waitingSleep(wakeIn([], now, now))` = sleep(Duration.zero) — busy loop? Future.any with a zero-duration sleep: the sleep completes immediately on the event loop; Future.wait for a running child takes 120ms real → the any resolves via the zero sleep → round "completes" instantly without waiting! Then steer liveness (no shell jobs → nothing), `if (isBusy)` — not busy → skip. Loop continues → 10 rounds in microseconds → cap → `_finishHeadlessDrain` → still active (child running) → prints detach message + detach summary → run EXITS while child still running! That breaks the legacy subagent drain!

Hmm wait — is that also true pre-PR? Pre-PR the subagent drain loop was:
```
for (var round...) { if (!jobsActive) break; await Future.any([...]); ... }
```
