The tail fetch: fetch once before loop (only if at least one steer will fire — minor; just fetch once when currentBucket > lastBucket && !probed).

Notice elapsed text: from `Duration(milliseconds: bucket * quietMs)` — normal cadence: wake lands exactly on threshold → elapsed ≈ bucket*quietMs → same text as before ('5m'). The existing IT expects '5m elapsed'/'10m elapsed' — with elapsed = exactly 5m: inMinutes=5 → '5m'. Good. But real-clock drain test (watchShape, drainMs 60ms): wakeIn pulls to 5m? wake = min(60ms, ~5m) = 60ms → sleep 60ms → elapsed=60ms → bucket 0 → no steer (quietMs default 5m > 60ms). Fine, notices there. Wait — actually in that test quietMs is default 3000, elapsed 60ms → bucket 0. OK.

