elapsedMs = 930000 = 15m30s. current=3, last=0 → loop buckets 1..3 → three notices. But the dump earlier showed only 2 runs. So the steer DID run with 3 buckets → 3 messages steered. But only 2 liveness RUNS observed?

The third notice: `_startRun` (bucket 1) then isBusy → `_agent.steer` ×2. Perhaps two of the steered notices got COALESCED into one run — e.g. the steer delivery batches multiple user messages into one context/run. The livenessRuns counter counts contexts; if notices 2 and 3 landed in the SAME context (one run carrying two steered user messages), the run's call-time last user text = the LAST steer ('15m') and there's only ONE context for two notices → livenessRuns=2 but 3 notices delivered!

Hmm, or the run for bucket 1 ('5m') ends so fast ('still waiting.') that by the time bucket-2's steer is processed the run already finished → bucket 2 starts a fresh run, bucket 3 steered into it... contexts: '5m' run, '10m'+'15m' run → livenessRuns counts both → 2 contexts but the second context's lastUserText = '15m' notice; the '10m' notice is the second-to-last user message in that context.

So "N notices ⇒ N runs" doesn't hold — steers into a busy run share one context. Is that acceptable for the ticket invariant "N crossings ⇒ exactly N notices (test counts)"? The notices ARE delivered (3 user messages). The count of notices in the transcript is 3; the count of RUNS is fewer. My test asserts run count == 3, which conflates runs with notices.

Better assertion: count the marker occurrences across all lastUserTexts? The '10m' notice text would be in context.messages but not as the LAST user message. Count occurrences of the marker clause across ALL user messages in all contexts:

```dart
int noticeCount = 0;
for (final c in stream.contexts) {
  for (final m in c.messages) {
    if (m is UserMessage && messageText(m).contains(_livenessMarker)) noticeCount++;
  }
```

But dedup: contexts may overlap (steered messages persist into continuation contexts!). The '5m' run's context, when continued, still contains the '5m' user message. If 'still waiting.' ends the turn, no continuation. But the bucket-2/3 steers: if they join a run whose context already contains '5m'... wait no — if bucket 1's run ended before bucket 2 steered, bucket 2 starts a NEW run: its context = prior messages + '10m' steer? How does steer-into-new-run work: `_startRun` — does the new run's context include previous transcript? Yes — the conversation is persisted; a new run replays the whole transcript. So the '10m' run's context CONTAINS the '5m' user message too! Counting marker occurrences across all contexts double-counts ('5m' appears in contexts 3, 4, ...).

Most robust: count occurrences in the FINAL transcript (last context) — it contains the full conversation. All 3 notices appear as user messages in the last context:

```dart
final lastTexts = [for (final m in stream.contexts.last.messages) if (m is UserMessage) messageText(m)];
expect(lastTexts.where((t) => t.contains(_livenessMarker)).length, 3);
